# ============================================================================
# 365step — environment
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. With none of them set, the app runs on a
# local SQLite file and the AI assistant uses its deterministic analysis, so
# `npm install && npm run db:seed && npm run dev` is genuinely all you need.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` to use any of them.
# ============================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- database ---
# Unset  ->  SQLite at ./data/365step.db. Zero setup, and what the demo uses.
# Set    ->  PostgreSQL. The schema in db/schema.sql is written in the subset
#            both dialects accept, so it applies unchanged.
#
# Supabase: Project settings -> Database -> Connection string -> URI.
# Use the pooled connection (port 6543) for serverless deploys such as Vercel.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.[ref]:[password]@aws-0-[region].pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# Where the SQLite file lives, if you want it somewhere else.
# SQLITE_PATH=./data/365step.db


# ------------------------------------------------------------------- the AI ---
# The AI Growth Assistant works without this: the analysis, the insights and the
# "what should I do today" suggestions are all computed from your own rows by a
# deterministic engine. A key only changes who writes the one-sentence headline
# above them — Claude instead of the rule-based writer. If the call fails or is
# refused, it falls back silently.
#
# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- deployment ---
# Only needed if something has to build absolute URLs. Vercel sets its own.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
